        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(msteams): add timeouts to file consent upload requests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nTeams file consent uploads validated the SharePoint consent URL, then performed the upload PUT without a request deadline. If the upload request never completed, the accepted file delivery path could remain pending indefinitely.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd a bounded consent upload timeout using the existing timer timeout resolver, and keep the abort timer active until the upload request finishes. The SSRF host/IP validation and upload headers/body semantics are unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nWhen a Teams file consent upload stalls, OpenClaw now aborts the request instead of waiting forever, so the file delivery flow can fail quickly and surface the error path.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/msteams/src/file-consent.test.ts` passed: 64 tests.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- `corepack pnpm exec oxlint --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.extensions.json extensions/msteams/src/file-consent.ts extensions/msteams/src/file-consent.test.ts` passed.\n- Remote Testbox/Crabbox validation was attempted, but the local wrapper rejected the selected crabbox binary during sanity checks, so focused local wrapper tests were used instead.\n",
        "branch": "alix/msteams-file-consent-upload-timeouts",
